From 03e744ad5476f7b6819d6e945ecc6012c0400a4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HOTTY Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 19:09:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] blitz-dom, blitz-paint: a document can lock scrolling along
 an axis

An embedder that shows a document in an area of a fixed size, and
scrolls it itself or not at all along some axis, needs the document to
keep still along that axis: a fragment link, an element brought into
view, a fling or a scrollbar drag must not move it, and no scrollbar may
promise that something would.

BaseDocument::set_scroll_axes locks an axis (both are unlocked by
default). Along a locked axis every scroll target's range is empty, so
every scroll, whoever asks, stays at zero, and locking puts the offsets
there. No overlay scrollbar is drawn or hit there. A text input still
scrolls its own text, which follows the caret.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs  | 39 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 packages/blitz-dom/src/scrolling.rs | 15 +++++++++++
 packages/blitz-paint/src/render.rs  |  2 +-
 3 files changed, 54 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

